+# Test Suite Optimization Notes
+
+## Baseline Metrics (2026-10-06)
+
+### Full `spec/models` (1795 examples)
+- **Baseline (Sidekiq inline, no optimizations):** 151.7s (2m31s), 0 failures, seed 50975
+- **With Sidekiq fake globally:** 123.1s (2m03s), 3 failures (email-related), seed 25984
+  - Saving: ~28.6s (18.9%)
+  - Failures:
+    - `spec/models/admin/account_action_spec.rb:90` (sends email to target account user)
+    - `spec/models/user_spec.rb:504` (mark_email_as_confirmed! delivers welcome email)
+    - `spec/models/email_subscription_spec.rb:30` (generates token and delivers confirmation email)
+  - All failures are `capture_emails` expecting `deliver_later` to execute inline.
+
+### Representative Files (with inline)
+- `spec/models/account_spec.rb` (122 examples): 4.17s
+- `spec/models/status_spec.rb` (62 examples): 8.51s (profile: tagged_with, ordered_media_attachments slowest)
+- `spec/models/media_attachment_spec.rb` (27 examples): 6.88s (mp3 2.44s, video 0.57s, gif 0.51s)
+- `spec/models/account/avatar_spec.rb` + header + custom_emoji + preview_card (26 examples): 1.57s
+
+### Factory Profiling (status_spec, with inline, via test-prof FPROF)
+- Total: 320 fabrications, 7.15s out of 9.9s (72% in factories)
+- status: 105, 4.53s (43ms each)
+- bookmark (nested, from status after_create): 105, 1.94s (18.5ms each) — INJECTED, to be fixed in factories phase
+- account: 70, 1.61s (23ms each)
+- media_attachment: 8, 0.55s (69ms each)
+- poll: 2, 0.236s (118ms each)
+
+### Factory Profiling (account_spec, with fake)
+- Total: 167 fabrications, 2.12s
+- account: 101, 1.60s (15.9ms each)
+- status: 18, 0.33s (18.6ms each)
+- bookmark (nested): 18, 0.22s (12.3ms each)
+- login_activity (nested, from user after_create): 12, 0.016s (1.4ms each) — INJECTED
+
+### Benchmarks (isolated Fabrication)
+- 20 accounts fake: 0.175s (8.7ms each), inline: 0.452s (22.6ms each) => overhead 14ms/account
+- 20 statuses inline: 0.957s (47ms each), fake: 0.448s (22ms each) => overhead 25ms/status
+- TriggerWebhookWorker perform: 17ms per job (DB query + AMS serialization 5.6ms)
+- MediaAttachment: 257ms each (VIPS + Paperclip, attachment.jpg)
+- CustomEmoji: 12ms each
+- PreviewCard: 30ms each (with image)
+- Faker::Internet.user_name: 0.5ms per call
+
+### SQL Profiling (status_spec, EVENT_PROF)
+- SQL: 0.843s of 5.13s (16.4%), 5329 events
+- DB is not the bottleneck; Ruby CPU + factories dominate.
+
+### StackProf (status_spec, cpu mode, with fake)
+- Fabrication: 55.5%
+- Validations (valid?, run_validations): 17.4%
+- GC: 15.9% (high allocation)
+- UniquenessValidator: 4.9%
+- Faker: 4.4% (user_name, email, etc.)
+- User#set_approved: 4.2% (requires_approval? checks)
+- UsernameBlock.matches?: 3.6%
+- BCrypt (password=): 3.5%
+- Paperclip: 1.6%, Vips: 0.7%
+- Sidekiq perform_async (fake): 0.7% (cheap)
+
+### Slowest Examples (full models, with fake, --profile 20)
+- MediaAttachment mp3: 2.65s
+- Trends::Statuses#refresh: 2.43s, 2.11s (24 reblogs per example!)
+- AccountStatusesCleanupPolicy: 12.16s total (36 examples, 0.33s avg)
+- TagFeed: 10.75s (33 examples)
+- MediaAttachment: 7.29s, PublicFeed: 7.58s, Notification: 5.61s
+
+## Optimization Plan for `spec/models` (Phase 1, no factory edits)
+
+### 1. Sidekiq: fake by default for models, inline opt-in via tag
+- Change `config.before { Sidekiq.testing!(:inline) }` to be conditional:
+  - Default inline for all, but fake for `type: :model` unless `:sidekiq_inline` tag.
+  - Add `config.after { Sidekiq::Worker.clear_all }` for fake mode to avoid leakage.
+- Tag the 3 email specs with `:sidekiq_inline`:
+  - `spec/models/admin/account_action_spec.rb` sends email test
+  - `spec/models/user_spec.rb` mark_email_as_confirmed! test
+  - `spec/models/email_subscription_spec.rb` callbacks test
+- Expected saving: ~19% (28s)
+
+### 2. Status validators stubbing (no model spec tests them)
+- `DisallowedHashtagsValidator` and `StatusLengthValidator` are only tested in `spec/validators/`, not `spec/models/`.
+- For `type: :model`, stub them to no-op to save 1 DB query + entity extraction per status.
+- Expected saving: ~5-8%? (need to measure)
+
+### 3. Username/Email block checks stubbing
+- `User#set_approved` does 3 checks per user creation:
+  - `sign_up_from_ip_requires_approval?` (no query when sign_up_ip nil, skip)
+  - `sign_up_email_requires_approval?` (EmailDomainBlock query)
+  - `sign_up_username_requires_approval?` (UsernameBlock query with allow_with_approval: true)
+- `UnreservedUsernameValidator` does UsernameBlock query with allow_with_approval: false (seeds have such blocks, account_spec tests 'support')
+- `UniqueUsernameValidator` does Account uniqueness query (account_spec tests the_Doctor)
+- `UserEmailValidator` skipped for confirmed users (most fabrications), no need.
+- Plan: Stub `EmailDomainBlock.requires_approval?`, `EmailDomainBlock.block?`, `UsernameBlock.matches?` with allow_with_approval:true to false, except for specs that test them (username_block_spec, email_domain_block_spec, ip_block_spec, confirmation_spec, account_spec validation examples).
+- Use tags to opt-out: e.g., `:username_blocks`, `:email_blocks`.
+- Expected saving: ~5-10%? (need to measure)
+
+### 4. ActivityTracker stubbing
+- Only `spec/models/user_spec.rb` tests ActivityTracker (with its own stub).
+- For `type: :model`, stub `ActivityTracker.increment` and `record` to no-op to save 2 redis commands per status.
+- Expected saving: ~2-3s? (need to measure)
+
+### 5. Redis clearing optimization (minor)
+- Current: `redis.del(redis.keys)` (KEYS * + DEL) per test.
+- Alternative: `redis.flushdb` — benchmark shows similar or slightly slower for small key counts, but more correct? Actually for 5 keys, both ~0.03ms per test, negligible. Skip or keep as is? Measure.
+- Total redis clearing overhead: ~54ms for 1795 tests, negligible. Not worth.
+
+### 6. Paperclip stubbing for non-media specs (future, measure first)
+- Only `spec/models/status_spec.rb` (8 attachments) and `account_statuses_cleanup_policy_spec.rb` (1 attachment) fabricate media_attachments outside media specs.
+- Saving would be ~0.5-1s, small. Defer unless needed.
+
+### Target
+- Baseline: 151.7s
+- Target (30-35% improvement): 98-106s (save 45-53s)
+- Sidekiq alone: 28s (19%), need additional 17-25s (11-16%) from validators + blocks + ActivityTracker.
+
+## Future Phases (not in this step)
+- Factories: status->bookmark after_create, user->login_activity after_create, announcement_reaction->custom_emoji, conversation parent_account Fabricate vs build, etc.
+- Requests: similar Sidekiq + validator optimizations, plus request-specific (host!, https!, signed requests, etc.)
+- Overall target: models + requests together 2x faster.
+
+## Notes
+- Do not touch `spec/fabricators/*` in this phase.
+- Do not touch other spec types (only `type: :model`).
+- What examples assert must stay the same; use tags + shared setup.
+- No app code changes affecting runtime behavior; only test setup stubs.
